# VM target configuration for remote-services/setup-vm.sh
#
# Copy this file to vm.env and change the values to switch to a different VM.
# Only 2–3 values usually need to change when moving providers.

# SSH target: a host alias from ~/.ssh/config or user@ip.
# Example aliases: aws-ssfx, azure-vm, gcp-ssfx
SSH_HOST=aws-ssfx

# Remote user on the VM. If SSH_HOST contains user@, this is auto-derived.
# VM_USER=ec2-user

# OS family for package installer selection. Auto-detected from /etc/os-release
# if omitted. Supported: amazonlinux, rhel, ubuntu.
# VM_OS_FAMILY=amazonlinux

# Remote deployment path (optional; default is ~/ssfx-remote-services).
# REMOTE_DIR=/home/ec2-user/ssfx-remote-services
